From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: refresh config.sub in MAKEBUILDDIR (macOS 15 / Darwin 24)

On macOS 15 the build triplet from `clang -dumpmachine` is
`arm64-apple-darwin24.6.0`. Old autotools contrib packages that do not
autoreconf (e.g. dvdcss) ship a config.sub predating Apple-Silicon `arm64`
support, so configure aborts with "config.sub arm64-apple-darwin24.6.0 failed".

Refresh config.sub/config.guess from the host automake in MAKEBUILDDIR, which
every out-of-source autotools package runs as a standalone recipe line before
MAKECONFIGURE. It must go in MAKEBUILDDIR, not MAKECONFIGURE: packages such as
gnutls prefix a cache variable onto MAKECONFIGURE (gl_cv_...=yes $(MAKECONFIGURE)),
and a leading $(UPDATE_AUTOCONFIG) for-loop there makes the shell reject
"VAR=value for ..." with 'Syntax error: do unexpected'. MAKEBUILDDIR is never
VAR-prefixed, so this is safe; no-op where config.sub is already fresh and on
non-Darwin toolchains.
---
--- a/contrib/src/main.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/main.mak
@@ -453,7 +453,7 @@
-MAKEBUILDDIR = mkdir -p $(BUILD_DIR) && rm -f $(BUILD_DIR)/config.status
+MAKEBUILDDIR = mkdir -p $(BUILD_DIR) && rm -f $(BUILD_DIR)/config.status && $(UPDATE_AUTOCONFIG)
 MAKEBUILD = $(MAKE) -C $(BUILD_DIR)
 MAKECONFDIR = cd $(BUILD_DIR) && $(HOSTVARS) $(BUILD_SRC)
 MAKECONFIGURE = $(MAKECONFDIR)/configure $(HOSTCONF)
 
 # Work around for https://lists.nongnu.org/archive/html/bug-gnulib/2020-05/msg00237.html
 # When using a single command, make might take a shortcut and fork/exec
